  (footprint "temper:Relay_SPST_Omron-G4A-E" (version 20231120) (generator temper-hand) (layer "F.Cu")
    (tedit dfffc6b5) (tstamp 0b982040-5316-4da5-e83f-acd4396bda7a)
    (at 94.61 85.75)
    (descr "Omron G4A-1A-E PCB power relay, #250 Faston quick-connect contacts + PCB coil terminals. Dimensions from official Omron datasheet (https://omronfs.omron.com/en_US/ecb/products/pdf/en-g4a.pdf, Cat. No. J056-E1-09, page 2 'Dimensions' section): body envelope 30.5 x 16 x 23.5mm max; coil pins (A1,A2) at 6.35mm pitch, standard 0.25in relay coil spacing; 4x mounting/locating holes, 1.8mm dia, in a 22mm(X) x 12mm(Y, asymmetric 6.25/5.75 split) pattern -- both sub-dimensions confirmed internally consistent (6.25+5.75=12.00mm exactly matches the datasheet's labeled 12mm total). Pad numbers match the real EN50005 relay pinout used by the placed KiCad symbol (Relay:Relay_SPST-NO): A1/A2 = coil, 13/14 = contacts (COM/NO). Contact terminals (13=COM, 14=NO) are #250 (6.35mm, SAE/AMP industry-standard width, not vendor-specific) Faston quick-connect tabs -- the datasheet's own Model Number Legend confirms both terminal-shape variants (E vs PE) share identical 'PCB coil terminals' wording and differ only in contact terminal type, so these tabs have zero PCB copper connection on this variant; they mate externally with a push-on spade connector, not a PCB trace. Modeled here as SMD (no-drill) landing pads purely for netlist/footprint pin-count parity and courtyard/placement-clearance purposes -- NOT a claim that solder-in-hole geometry exists at these exact coordinates. Relative layout (tabs on the opposite long edge from the coil row, mirroring the coil's left/right split) is taken directly from the datasheet's own Terminal Arrangement diagram; the tabs' precise Y-offset from the coil row is a reasonable placement within the confirmed courtyard bounds, not a measured value -- verify against the physical part before hand-soldering wires to pads 13/14. Mounting holes are NPTH (mechanical only, no net); their pattern's position relative to the coil pins is datasheet-derived from a linearized reading, not a pixel-exact trace -- cross-check against the datasheet page 2 drawing before fabrication.")
    (tags "relay SPST G4A Omron power relay")
    (property "Reference" "K1")
    (property "Value" "?")
    (property "Footprint" "temper:Relay_SPST_Omron-G4A-E")
    (attr through_hole)
    (fp_rect (start -15.25 -11.75) (end 15.25 11.75) (layer "F.CrtYd") (width 0.05) (fill none))
    (fp_rect (start -15.25 -11.75) (end 15.25 11.75) (layer "F.SilkS") (width 0.12) (fill none))
    (pad "A1" thru_hole circle (at -3.175 0) (size 1.8 1.8) (drill 1) (layers *.Cu *.Mask)
      (net 31 "coil1"))
    (pad "A2" thru_hole circle (at 3.175 0) (size 1.8 1.8) (drill 1) (layers *.Cu *.Mask)
      (net 32 "coil2"))
